Let me look at the actual bug. The issue says: "xmlXIncludeLoadTxt (xinclude.c) can end up calling xmlStaticCopyNode (tree.c) on a node that has already been freed (by the XML reader code)".

Let me look at the `xmlCopyNode` call in `xmlXIncludeLoadTxt`. At line ~1857:
```c
    for (i = 0; i < ctxt->txtNr; i++) {
        if (xmlStrEqual(URL, ctxt->txturlTab[i])) {
            node = xmlCopyNode(ctxt->txtTab[i], 1);
            goto loaded;
        }
    }
```

So `xmlCopyNode(ctxt->txtTab[i], 1)` is called on a node that has already been freed. The `ctxt->txtTab[i]` is a text node that was stored earlier. The issue is that the node stored in `ctxt->txtTab[i]` was freed by the XML reader code.

